  "summary": "Four database updates and one new database extend prokaryotic and phage genomic annotation with taxonomic, structural and environmental context.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is curated, searchable resources that connect microbial and phage sequence data to annotation layers. BGC Atlas v2 covers over 16 million predicted biosynthetic gene clusters with taxonomic, environmental and geographic search. mOTUs-db links taxonomy, genome-encoded function and biogeography, with a CLI and API for profiling. P2CS-Web relates two-component system repertoires to domain architectures, genomic neighbourhoods and sequence clusters. PhageScope 2.0 is described as a million-scale resource integrating phage genomic, functional and structural diversity. LPMOcat, a preprint, adds structural annotation for 161 characterised lytic polysaccharide monooxygenases. Novelty lies in scale and contextual integration, not in new typing algorithms; the items do not report genomic typing workflows.",
